[[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Pull back the upper part of the headrest while lifting it completely.</p><p>2. Wheel the pins (about 45°) and remove the headrest.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2019395.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Make sure that the headrest\nis not damaged.</p><p>1. Wheel the pins (1a) so as to bring the notches (1b) on the front\nside.</p><p>2. Replace the headrest into its seat.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2019396.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]]